  "description": "The Audio 24” builds on the foundation of the Audio 22”, stepping up to a larger wheel size designed for taller riders, returning BMX riders, and anyone looking for a more spacious setup that still rides like a proper BMX. At its core is a full chromoly aftermarket-spec frame and fork, delivering the same durability and detail as the rest of the Audio line, with geometry carefully adjusted to keep the ride responsive and engaging. With newly developed 24” specific parts such as the Logic rim and Overbite tyre, it’s built to handle trails, street riding, or fast, casual sessions with ease. The Audio 24” bridges the gap between comfort and true BMX feel—familiar, but with more room to ride.",
